# less — real-world examples

## Don't clear the screen on exit

```sh
less -X file.log
```

## Columnize output before paging

```sh
dpkg -l | pr --columns 3 -l 60 | less -X
```

## Follow a file as it grows (like tail -f, but scrollable)

```sh
less +F /var/log/messages     # Ctrl+C to stop following, F to resume
```

## Homelab: page a huge Plex log on mediaserver with search

```sh
ssh david@mediaserver 'cat "/var/lib/plex/Plex Media Server/Logs/Plex Media Server.log"' | less -N
# inside less: /error to search forward, n = next match, N = previous
```

## Homelab: keep color codes from zypper/rg output

```sh
rg --color=always -n 'ERROR' /var/log | less -R
```

## Jump around inside less

```
g   top of file          G   end of file
/pattern  search fwd     ?pattern  search back
&pattern  show only matching lines
q   quit
```

| Flag | What it does                          |
| ---- | ------------------------------------- |
| -X   | no screen clear on exit               |
| -R   | pass ANSI colors through              |
| -N   | show line numbers                     |
| -S   | chop long lines instead of wrapping   |
| +F   | follow mode (tail -f style)           |
| -i   | case-insensitive search               |
